Package: SIGA
Type: Package
Title: Subgroup Identification Based on a Genetic Algorithm
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Liang", "Zhao", email = "wethenwethen@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Identifies subgroups of patients with an enhanced treatment
    effect in two-arm randomised clinical trials with the SIGA method
    (subgroup identification based on a genetic algorithm) of Zhao et al.
    (2024) <doi:10.1080/10543406.2023.2170397>. Candidate
    subgroups are encoded as real-valued chromosomes whose genes define
    biomarker thresholds or level sets, are scored by the
    treatment-by-subgroup interaction p-value, and evolve with the
    selection, recombination and mutation operators of the 'gatbxr'
    toolbox in several isolated sub-populations. A resampling scheme
    controls multiplicity (false subgroup discovery) and complexity (noise
    biomarkers). Time-to-event, binary and continuous endpoints are
    supported, together with biomarker prescreening, cross-validation,
    parallel computing and the simulation models used to evaluate the
    method.
